Radiological investigations for urethral stricture are :-
	(1) Retrograde urethrography; 
	(2) Micturating cystourethrography; 
	(3) Endoscopy (urethroscopy); 
	(4) Sonographic urethrogram; 
	(5) High frequency USG.

Characteristic feature of gallstone ileus is Rigler's triad :

Incomplete or complete small bowel obstruction; 
Gas in biliary tree; 
Ectopic gallstone.

Information is this question are :-
	1) Exposure to textile industry; 
	2) Reticulo-nodular pattern in lower lung zone; 
	3) Loss of definition of heart border and diphragm; 
	4) Small pleural effusion. 
	​All these suggest the diagnosis of asbestosis.

Central Dot sign on CT or USG is seen in:

Caroli's disease (most common cause); 
Prebiliary cysts; 
Obstructive jaundice; and 
Periportal lymphedema.
